    "response": "{\"decision\":\"established_flaw\",\"issues\":[{\"category\":\"unsupported_inference\",\"target_kind\":\"assertion\",\"claim_quote\":\"Policy debate functions as a generalized rupture in civic selfhood and social order across the packet.\",\"evidence\":[{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_b89250c86251f1b6\",\"quote\":\"On the back of all the discussions we have been having today, it is written in statute that within 56 days the Mayor of London and the Commissioner of the Metropolitan Police will have to respond with an action plan to deal with all the issues we have talked about today.\"}],\"whole_packet_no_support\":\"whole_packet_no_support\",\"mechanism\":\"The excerpt discusses a statutory response plan, not a generalized rupture of civic selfhood or social order.\",\"material_consequence\":\"The claim makes a broad, unsupported assertion about the impact of policy debate, lacking evidentiary support.\",\"counterconditions\":\"The evidence focuses on a specific legislative response, not a fundamental disruption of societal structures.\"}],\"unresolved\":[],\"rationale\":\"The claim asserts a broad, consequential impact of policy debate that is not supported by the provided evidence, which details a specific statutory response. The evidence does not warrant the claim's generalization about 'civic selfhood and social order'.\"}",
